&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Creator Channel Manager owns the strategic direction and end-to-end performance of the Creator channel. This is a hybrid role spanning strategy, operations, analytics, and stakeholder management — not purely creator execution. The channel has evolved significantly: operational sourcing has largely shifted to the agency, while the FTE focus has moved to strategic steering, quality control, performance analysis, and channel development. With the Creative Strategist now owning creative strategy, this role focuses on what only a senior channel owner can do: agency steering, incentivization innovation, amplification strategy, and cross-functional channel development.&lt;/p&gt;
